cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "mndsim: a mechanistic motor-unit degeneration simulator for ALS/MND"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Taranjeet Singh
    family-names: Matharu
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-15
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ProudStone-576/motor-unit-degeneration-simulator"
keywords:
  - amyotrophic lateral sclerosis
  - motor neuron disease
  - motor unit
  - disease progression model
  - in-silico clinical trial
  - computational neuroscience
abstract: >-
  mndsim simulates motor neuron disease from single motor units to virtual
  clinical trials. It models a size-ordered motor-unit pool per body region,
  selective vulnerability, dying-back denervation, collateral reinnervation,
  upper-motor-neuron loss with excitotoxic drive and contiguous spread, and
  derives functional scores, FVC, motor unit number estimates, CMAP and
  survival. It supports counterfactual treatments, heterogeneous virtual
  cohorts, power analysis for randomised trials, fitting of digital twins
  and global sensitivity analysis.
